WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:10.930
50. Save Our Seas In August 2000, people in the Australian seaside

2
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:17.130
town of Cairns found something very unusual on their beach. A whale. It was sick and had

3
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:23.730
come out of the ocean. It soon died on the sand. When vets looked inside the dead whale,

4
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:29.410
they found six square meters of plastic. The animal had eaten plastic bags that humans

5
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:35.810
had thrown into the sea. Another whale died in Terschling in the Netherlands in 2013.

6
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:41.770
It had swallowed plastic bags, rope, flower pots, and even a spray bottle. Turtles eat

7
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:46.610
plastic bags all the time, mistaking them for jellyfish.

8
00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:53.510
In May 2003, a platypus was found near a river in Tasmania, an Australian island. A plastic

9
00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:59.910
bag was wrapped around its body. It survived and was named lucky by its rescuers. Sadly,

10
00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.590
many other platypuses are not so lucky.

11
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:08.910
Animals are dying because of our trash. Plastic bags are a particular problem because they

12
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:15.150
last such a long time. While paper bags break down in months, plastic bags take a minimum

13
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:21.990
of ten years, but they are light and cheap and people use them every day without thinking.

14
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:27.110
Many countries have tried to manage the problem of plastic bags. Bangladesh was the first

15
00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:33.750
country to ban them, and others, including China, have adopted full or partial bans.

16
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.270
Governments have asked people to use cloth bags at the supermarket instead.

17
00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.990
We cannot solve this problem overnight. There is already too much plastic in our oceans.

18
00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:50.470
However, we can stop producing more. Plastic comes from natural gas and petrol, which are

19
00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:56.470
bad for the environment anyway. Both humans and animals will benefit if plastic bags are

20
00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:57.670
banned everywhere.
